#message 26 "King Brannoc is in the great hall, across the drawbridge."
#message 27 "The path leaves the drawbridge and runs east into the meadows."
#message 28 "Old trees crowd the west side of the gate. Nothing is hiding in them except a few birds."
#message 29 "A thick hedge, taller than the gardener and better kept."
#message 30 "You stop at the edge of the meadow. Leaving without the king's errand would just be a walk, and the notice is still on the board."
#message 31 "That's somewhere out in the countryside, not here at the gate."
#message 32 "The Three Bright Things are somewhere out in the countryside. The notice says what to look for."
#message 33 "There are no candles to light here at the gate."
#message 34 "One window in the east tower glows. The last candle in Thornwall burns behind it."
#message 35 "The red pennant of Thornwall, faded to the color of an old brick."
#message 36 "Far to the east, smoke rises from a crooked chimney."
#message 37 "A mild, clear morning."
#message 38 "Daisies and buttercups. The meadow grows right up to the gate."
#message 39 "You would like to keep both hands."
#message 40 "The alligator would sooner take you."
#message 41 "You have nothing to carry water in, and the alligator is using it."
#message 42 "You already have it."
#message 43 "Walk north across the drawbridge to reach the gate."
#message 44 "The notice is pinned flat to the board. You can't see the back from here."
#message 45 "The bench stays where it is."

